## Referências
<br>
Estas são as principais fontes utilizadas como referência geral para a elaboração do material sobre planejamento, coleta de evidências e aquisição de memória. Todos os acessos às fontes foram realizados em 10/08/2026.
<br>
1. **Brezinski, D.; Killalea, T. — RFC 3227: Guidelines for Evidence Collection and Archiving (2002).**  
   https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3227.html

2. **Kent, K.; Chevalier, S.; Grance, T.; Dang, H. — NIST SP 800-86: Guide to Integrating Forensic Techniques into Incident Response (2006).**  
   https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/Legacy/SP/nistspecialpublication800-86.pdf

3. **Nelson, A.; Rekhi, S.; Souppaya, M.; Scarfone, K. — NIST SP 800-61 Rev. 3: Incident Response Recommendations and Considerations for Cybersecurity Risk Management (2025).**  
   https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/61/r3/final

4. **Fabro, M.; Cornelius, E. — Recommended Practice: Creating Cyber Forensics Plans for Control Systems (2008).**  
   https://www.cisa.gov/sites/default/files/recommended_practices/Forensics_RP.pdf

5. **SWGDE — Best Practices for Computer Forensic Acquisitions (17-F-002-2.1).**  
   https://www.swgde.org/?attachment_id=5868&swpmtx=3e217fe751b710f55510d5fc2b47083e&swpmtxnonce=c4e6c8e8fd

6. **SWGDE — Best Practices for Digital Evidence Collection (18-F-002-2.0).**  
   https://www.swgde.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/2025-11-20-Best-Practices-for-Digital-Evidence-Collection-18-F-002-2.0.pdf

7. **Rzepka et al. — A scenario-based quality assessment of memory acquisition tools and its investigative implications (2025).**  
   *Forensic Science International: Digital Investigation*, Vol. 52.  
  https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2666281725000071

8. **Belkasoft — RAM Forensics: Tools, Techniques, and Best Practices.**  
   https://belkasoft.com/ram-forensics-tools-techniques

9. **CyberDefenders — Why Memory Forensics Matters in Modern Cybersecurity?**  
   https://cyberdefenders.org/blog/what-is-memory-forensics

10. **DFIR Assist — Forensic Acquisition Guide: 103 acquisition methods across 5 platforms.**  
    https://forge-work.com/dfir/acquisition
